The data files in src/main/resources/org/tauasa/faux/data/ (bundled in
the jar) and tools/data/extra/ (in the source repository only) were built on
2026-11-19 and 2026-11-20 by the scripts in tools/data/ from these sources.
Each file's first line gives its build date.

1. Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org), CC0 1.0, queried through the QLever
   endpoint (https://qlever.dev) and the Wikidata Query Service.
   - every *_first_names.txt and *_surnames.txt file: given and family names
     ranked by how many people of each citizenship carry them. The South
     Korean files pair each name's Korean (Hangul) label with its most common
     romanization.
   - us_companies_domains.txt: company names, headquarters and official
     websites.

2. GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org), licensed under the Creative Commons
   Attribution 4.0 License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
   - us_cities_states_zip.txt, in tools/data/extra/: US postal codes and populated places
     (export/zip/US.zip, export/dump/cities1000.zip).
   - us_street_names_city_state_zip.txt: the city and state for each ZIP code.
   - us_companies_domains.txt: headquarters coordinates resolved to a city.
   Changes: places were sampled per state, joined to postal codes, and reduced
   to name, state and one ZIP code.

3. US Census Bureau, TIGER/Line Shapefiles 2024, Address Features (ADDRFEAT).
   A work of the US Government, not subject to copyright in the United States.
   - us_street_names_city_state_zip.txt: street names and ZIP codes.

Each data file's selection method is described in SPEC.md and in the
docstring of the script that builds it.
